-0.44703972339630127], [" Intel", -1.5819218158721924]]}, {"t": " Intel", "lp": -0.08612716943025589, "top": [[" Intel", -0.08612716943025589], [" **", -3.3135974407196045]]}, {"t": " one", "lp": -1.0513683557510376, "top": [[" one", -1.0513683557510376], [" SY", -1.2761322259902954]]}, {"t": "API", "lp": -0.5929527878761292, "top": [["API", -0.5929527878761292], [" compilers", -1.903248906135559]]}, {"t": " D", "lp": -0.5639573931694031, "top": [[" D", -0.5639573931694031], [" compilers", -0.9974329471588135]]}, {"t": "PC", "lp": -0.0003341994888614863, "top": [["PC", -0.0003341994888614863], ["pc", -8.370071411132812]]}, {"t": "++", "lp": -0.0002641430764924735, "top": [["++", -0.0002641430764924735], ["+/", -8.5314302444458]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function \u2014 Step by Step\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line. Note that the function appears to be **cut off** at the end (the last `-DGGML_SYCL_DEVICE` flag is incomplete), so I'll explain what's shown and flag the truncation.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (paths to `icx`/`icpx` compilers, libraries, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it thinks it's already configured. Without this, the SYCL compilers wouldn't be on your `PATH`.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nStops the script immediately if any command returns a non-zero exit code. Standard safety for build scripts.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja \\\n```\n- `-S`: source directory (the cloned repo)\n- `-B`: build directory\n- `-G Ninja`: use the Ninja build generator (fast, referenced in `makedepends`)\n\n```bash\n    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n```\nOptimized build (enables `-O3`-style optimizations, strips debug info \u2014 consistent with `!debug` in options).\n\n```bash\n    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib \\\n```\nWhere files get installed: `/usr`, with libraries going to `/usr/lib`.\n\n```bash\n    -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx \\\n```\n**The key flag.** Forces the Intel oneAPI DPC++"}